# TODO - Parametric compiler challenge generator

## Objective

Build deterministic source-level workload generators whose difficulty can grow
continuously instead of saturating at one application-specific threshold. The
bounded P1 milestone covers sixteen replayable C/oracle topologies spanning
arithmetic, ternary transforms, DAGs, control flow, calls, memory and aliasing,
streaming state, graph/tree reduction, layout pressure, nested state, and mixed
composition. Every instance is identified by family, version, seed, target
profile, and explicit difficulty parameters so algorithms can be compared on the
same problem rather than on vaguely similar examples.

**Completion boundary.** The generator milestone ends at deterministic admitted
C plus independent semantic oracle, canonical manifest, profile binding,
normalized-frontend evidence, native-oracle agreement, and large replay stress.
Final `.malbolge` execution is owned by the versioned C/Malbolge corpus
after the layout backend and translation validation exist.
Synthesis-specific challenge axes such as self-modification footprint, layout
coupling, target-state entropy,
and reusable-block coverage are owned by the empirical synthesis scaling study.
They are not prerequisites for completing this reusable source/oracle substrate.

**Current implementation.**

- `benchmarks/challenges/generate.py` implements deterministic
  `arithmetic-dag/v1`, `linear-mix/v1`, `branch-mix/v1`, `binary-tree/v1`,
  `memory-walk/v1`, `call-chain/v1`, `pointer-walk/v1`, `alias-walk/v1`, and
  `stream-state/v1`, `sort-reduce/v1`, `graph-reduce/v1`,
  `grid-accumulate/v1`, `layout-chain/v1`, `ternary-fold/v1`,
  `nested-state/v1`, and `composed-pipeline/v1` challenges
  identified by family,
  version, unsigned seed,
  canonical target-profile fingerprint, and node count. Every node feeds the
  next node on a live dependency spine so difficulty cannot grow through dead C
  statements. The domain-separated linear family is a strict predecessor
  chain while the DAG family retains additional source-order fan-in. The
  branch family adds one live `if`/`else` diamond per node. The memory family
  uses a fixed eight-cell local array with deterministic indexed read/write/read

  operations per node. The call family threads the live value through one pure
  three-argument helper call per node. `composed-pipeline/v1` combines a live
  loop, state-selected local-memory access, one branch, and two helper calls per
  node so whole-program-style heterogeneous pressure grows on one result path.
- Each identity emits `program.c`, `oracle.bin`, and canonical `manifest.json`
  bytes. The manifest binds source/oracle SHA-256 digests, while the source
  entry
  `malbolge_challenge` returns the full oracle `uint32_t` without unavailable
  guest libc calls.
- Analysis evidence locks byte-identical replay and hash-locked v1 vectors under
  immutable `malbolge-2026.3` identity for
  `arithmetic-dag`, `pointer-walk`, `stream-state`, `sort-reduce`,
  `graph-reduce`, `grid-accumulate`, `binary-tree`, `layout-chain`,
  `ternary-fold`, `nested-state`, and `composed-pipeline`; difficulty growth
  covers all sixteen topologies,
  invalid identity rejection, non-destructive no-replace publication
  including a raced final-path collision, ABI/libc admission, and pinned-Clang
  agreement between emitted C and the independent Python oracle for all sixteen
  families. The
  normalized frontend additionally preserves the branch family’s expected
  `if-statement` count, the memory family’s exact array-subscript count, and
  one helper call per call-family node. `pointer-walk/v1` selects one array
  slot from the live value through a local pointer on every node; normalized
  frontend evidence retains one runtime-dependent subscript, one pointer
  declaration, and address/read/write unary operations per node. `alias-walk/v1`
  adds two runtime-selected pointers per node; those pointers may alias the same
  cell and the independent oracle preserves the emitted sequential write order.
  `stream-state/v1` uses `nodes` as deterministic stream length under a
  seed-stable transition rule, retaining one live `for` loop, one indexed token

  read, and one state-dependent branch in normalized frontend evidence.
  `sort-reduce/v1` adds data-dependent compare/swap work over a node-scaled
  item vector followed by a live sorted fold. Its Python oracle uses independent
  host sorting; normalized evidence retains three loops, one branch, and five
  live subscripts, while pinned Clang matches at 1, 64, and 257 nodes.
  `graph-reduce/v1` generates one acyclic parent link and weight per vertex;
  runtime reduction keeps parent-index and predecessor-state dependencies live,
  with normalized evidence retaining one loop and six graph/state subscripts.
  `binary-tree/v1` places every generated leaf in a fixed heap and reduces

  internal parents bottom-up, adding hierarchical fan-in without dead leaves.
  Normalized frontend evidence retains two loops and seven live subscripts;
  pinned Clang matches the independent oracle at 1, 64, and 257 nodes.
  `grid-accumulate/v1` emits a node-scaled token vector but executes an exact
  `nodes * nodes` live accumulation loop nest. Generator and oracle work remain
  linear because the independent oracle uses the closed-form modulo-`2^32`
  sum; normalized frontend evidence retains two loops and one token subscript,
  while pinned Clang agrees with the oracle at 257 nodes.
  `layout-chain/v1` emits one distinct live helper function and call target per
  node, so function/code-layout pressure grows without dead source blocks;

  normalized evidence retains `nodes + 2` functions and `nodes + 1` calls.
  `ternary-fold/v1` keeps state and tokens inside the classic ten-trit domain
  and performs explicit base-three quotient/remainder mixing before folding the
  node-scaled token stream; native evidence matches the Python oracle.

  `nested-state/v1` adds a node-scaled token stream around a fixed four-lane
  inner state loop, so every node drives four live state transitions while
  generator/oracle construction remains linear in `nodes`. Normalized frontend
  evidence retains exactly two loops and three indexed reads; pinned Clang also
  matches the independent oracle at 4,096 nodes. `composed-pipeline/v1` has a
  hash-locked v1 replay vector plus native agreement at 1, 64, and 257 nodes;
  normalized evidence retains one loop, one branch, nine live subscripts, and
  three calls.
  Generation-only stress replays `stream-state`, `sort-reduce`, `graph-reduce`,
  `binary-tree`, `grid-accumulate`, `ternary-fold`, `nested-state`, and
  `composed-pipeline` byte-identically at
  16,384 nodes, retaining
  exact manifest

  difficulty and the fixed four-byte oracle without a wall-clock claim.
- The bounded generator objective is complete. Target-native
  block-synthesis/self-modification workloads and compiled/executed Malbolge
  fixtures remain downstream work under the owners named in the completion
  boundary; this record makes no claim that those capabilities already exist.

## Acceptance

- Every challenge has stable family/version/seed/profile identity, an oracle,
  and difficulty parameters that can scale beyond trivial saturation while
  remaining reproducible.
- Generated C and oracle bytes remain independently reproducible and admissible
  without requiring an unfinished target backend to certify this substrate.
- The work states a falsifiable question or hypothesis, an explicit baseline,
  and an observation that would reject or materially weaken the proposed
  technique before performance conclusions are accepted.
- If executable algorithm research is required, the stable ID is mirrored under
  `docs/research/algorithms/<id>/` and `algorithms/<id>/`; ordinary product
  engineering is not forced into that mirror.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Completed on 2026-09-04 after sixteen deterministic families, immutable
  replay identity, normalized/frontend and native-oracle evidence, large replay
  stress, and explicit downstream ownership transfer were validated.

